---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="container article-page">
    <div class="eyebrow">about</div>
    <h1> >> Hello, Cami</h1>
    <p class="article-lead"><em>Curious, open-minded and slightly hyperactive</em></p>

    <div class="prose about-prose">
      <p class="line">
        <span class="prompt">&gt;&gt;</span> I'm a young woman with way too many interests,
        a suspicious number of unfinished side projects,
        and very little ability to look at an idea and think,
        "maybe I don't need to do anything with this."
      </p>

      <p class="line">
        <span class="prompt">&gt;&gt;</span> I'm almost incapable of leaving a question alone.
        If something catches my attention, I tend to go a little too far with it,
        whether it's philosophy, technology, art, psychology, current events,
        or some completely random idea I stumbled across at 1 a.m.
        I like connecting things, questioning my own assumptions,
        and trying to understand not only what I think, but why I think it.
      </p>

      <p class="line">
        <span class="prompt">&gt;&gt;</span> On the technical side, I have a particular weakness for
        distributed systems, AI, infrastructure, DevOps, data engineering,
        GPUs, LLMs, and pretty much anything hidden behind an abstraction
        that makes me stop and ask:
        "wait... what is this actually doing?"
      </p>

      <p class="line">
        <span class="prompt">&gt;&gt;</span> I have a habit of turning new interests into projects, experiments,
        or slightly unnecessary challenges. Build an image search engine? Sure.
        Redis in C++? Educational. A fishing game that fits inside an Altoids tin?
        Somehow valid. Learn whittling because software wasn't giving me enough ways
        to accidentally hurt my hands? Also yes.
      </p>

      <p class="line">
        <span class="prompt">&gt;&gt;</span> I like hackathons, games, music, whittling,
        obscure technical rabbit holes, and projects that start with
        "this shouldn't be too hard" and somehow end with me reading
        documentation I didn't know existed three days earlier.
      </p>

      <p class="line">
        <span class="prompt">&gt;&gt;</span> I'm much more interested in figuring things out
        than pretending I already know them.
        Conveniently, the world gives me an endless supply of things to figure out.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
